// Greb (product: Mindforward) — Prisma schema. Spec source: prisma/spec/schema.full.prisma; deviations follow
// docs/00-beslutninger.md § 10a (ModuleTrack join, certificate opt-in, invitation/org fields). Prisma 7, PostgreSQL on Neon AWS Frankfurt).
// Canonical entity names: docs/00-beslutninger.md §9. Field docs: docs/03-datamodel.md.
//
// Conventions
// - Tables are snake_case via @@map; columns keep Prisma camelCase (Better Auth reads Prisma field names).
// - Every org-owned row carries organizationId and every query filters on it (src/server/auth/scope.ts).
// - Money: integer øre (prices) or Decimal(12,4) DKK (AI/content cost). Never Float for money.
// - Prompt free text (StepResult.promptText/aiFeedback, SandboxEvent.contentText) is deleted after 30 days
//   by the Inngest job `retention.purge-prompt-text`. Admin queries must never select these fields.
//
// Prisma 7 notes (verify at project start):
// - datasource `url` lives in prisma.config.ts (DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED for CLI/migrations).
// - Runtime client needs a driver adapter (@prisma/adapter-neon or @prisma/adapter-pg) with DATABASE_URL (pooled).
//
// Better Auth tables (User, Session, Account, Verification, TwoFactor, RateLimit, Organization, Membership,
// Invitation) follow the Better Auth core + organization plugin schema as documented 12 Oct 2026.
// TODO(M1): run `npx auth@latest generate` against this file and diff — Better Auth's CLI is the source of truth
// for its own fields. Organization plugin must be configured with schema.member.modelName = "membership"
// and custom roles named exactly OWNER | ADMIN | LEARNER (creatorRole: "OWNER") so writes match MembershipRole.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../src/generated/prisma"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

